[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Fully Insured]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.29]Lesson 43 | 第43课
[00:03.01]Fully insured | 全保险
[00:10.94]Who owned the pie dish and why? | 那只馅饼盘是谁的？为什么？
[00:15.55]Insurance companies are normally willing to insure anything. | 保险公司通常愿意承保任何东西。
[00:20.85]Insuring public or private property is a standard practice in most countries in the world. | 为公共财产或私人财产保险是世界上大多数国家的正常业务。
[00:28.14]If, however, you were holding an open air garden party or a fete it would be equally possible to insure yourself in the event of bad weather. | 然而，如果你举办露天游园会或盛宴的话，同样也可以为恶劣天气保险。
[00:40.27]Needless to say, the bigger the risk an insurance company takes, the higher the premium you will have to pay. | 不用说，保险公司承担的风险越大，你要付的保险费就越高。
[00:49.90]It is not uncommon to hear that a shipping company has made a claim for the cost of salvaging a sunken ship. | 轮船公司为打捞沉船的费用提出索赔，这是常有的事。
[00:58.02]But the claim made by a local authority to recover the cost of salvaging a sunken pie dish must surely be unique. | 但某地方当局为打捞一只沉入水中的馅饼盘的费用提出索赔，则肯定是独一无二的。
[01:08.34]Admittedly it was an unusual pie dish, for it was eighteen feet long and six feet wide. | 诚然，那是一只不寻常的馅饼盘，因为它长18英尺、宽6英尺。
[01:17.40]It had been purchased by a local authority so that an enormous pie could be baked for an annual fair. | 它是由一家地方当局购买的，以便在一年一度的集市上烤制一块巨大的馅饼。
[01:26.40]The pie committee decided that the best way to transport the dish would be by canal so they insured it for the trip. | 馅饼委员会决定用运河来运输这只盘子的方式最合适，于是他们为这次运输保了险。
[01:36.61]Shortly after it was launched, the pie committee went to a local inn to celebrate. | 盘子下水后不久，馅饼委员会成员们去当地一家小酒馆庆祝。
[01:43.28]At the same time, a number of teenagers climbed on to the dish and held a little party of their own. | 与此同时，一群十几岁的孩子爬上了盘子，开起了他们自己的小聚会。
[01:51.27]Dancing proved to be more than the dish could bear, | 结果表明，跳舞超出了盘子所能承受的，
[01:55.25]for during the party it capsized and sank in seven feet of water. | 因为聚会进行之中，盘子倾覆，沉入了7英尺深的水中。
[02:01.76]The pie committee telephoned a local garage owner who arrived in a recovery truck to salvage the pie dish. | 馅饼委员会给当地一家汽车修理厂老板打了电话，他开着一辆抢修车来打捞馅饼盘。
[02:10.67]Shivering in their wet clothes, the teenagers looked on while three men dived repeatedly into the water to locate the dish. | 孩子们穿着湿衣服直打哆嗦，在一旁观看3名工人一次又一次潜入水中寻找盘子。
[02:21.41]They had little difficulty in finding it, but hauling it out of the water proved to be a serious problem. | 他们毫不费力就找到了盘子，但把它拖出水面却成了一个难题。
[02:30.27]The sides of the dish were so smooth that it was almost impossible to attach hawsers and chains to the rim without damaging it. | 盘子四壁十分光滑，几乎不可能在不损坏盘子的前提下把缆绳和链条固定在盘沿上。
[02:42.12]Eventually chains were fixed to one end of the dish and a powerful winch was put into operation. | 最终，链条被固定在盘子的一端，一台大功率的绞车开始运转。
[02:50.84]The dish rose to the surface and was gently drawn towards the canal bank. | 盘子升出水面，被缓缓地拖向运河岸边。
[02:58.10]For one agonizing moment, the dish was perched precariously on the bank of the canal, | 在令人焦灼的一瞬间，盘子摇摇欲坠地立在运河岸边，
[03:05.67]but it suddenly overbalanced and slid back into the water. | 但它突然失去了平衡，滑回水中。
[03:11.34]The men were now obliged to try once more. | 工人们只得再试一次。
[03:15.82]This time they fixed heavy metal clamps to both sides of the dish so that they could fasten the chains. | 这一次，他们在盘子两侧固定了沉重的金属夹具，以便系住链条。
[03:24.77]The dish now had to be lifted vertically because one edge was resting against the side of the canal. | 此时必须垂直吊起盘子，因为盘子的一侧正抵靠着运河岸边。
[03:32.23]The winch was again put into operation and one of the men started up the truck. | 绞车再次开动，一名工人发动了卡车。
[03:38.89]Several minutes later, the dish was successfully hauled above the surface of the water. | 几分钟后，盘子被成功地吊出了水面。
[03:45.30]Water streamed in torrents over its sides with such force that it set up a huge wave in the canal. | 水流如瀑布般从盘子两侧倾泻而下，力量之大，在运河里掀起一股巨浪。
[03:53.96]There was a danger that the wave would rebound off the other side of the bank and send the dish plunging into the water again. | 巨浪有从对岸反弹回来、把盘子再次掀入水中的危险。
[04:04.44]By working at tremendous speed, the men managed to get the dish on to dry land before the wave returned. | 工人们以极快的速度干活，赶在浪头打回之前把盘子弄上了岸。
